+// wwe2k14 patch (Session 7b, GPUMARKS): GPU timestamps per frame-anatomy row (gpu_anatomy_gpu_marks). Measurement
+// only: timestamp writes into a query pool of their own and resets of those queries at the start of command
+// buffers; nothing that is emulated, drawn or presented changes. Pool layout: see GpuMarks.
+// The marks (bottom-of-pipe, so written once all of the queue's earlier work has completed, except cb_begin):
+//   cb_begin   top-of-pipe, the command buffer's first command (after the query resets)
+//   pre        IssueDraw, right after SubmitBarriersAndEnterRenderTargetCacheRenderPass: the draw's uploads,
+//              texture loads, barriers and render pass changes are all recorded before it
+//   post       right after the draw call
+//   before / after   IssueCopy, around the whole resolve (no `after` if the readback path ended the submission:
+//              then the submission's cb_end, right after the copy's commands, is the copy's end)
+//   cb_end     the command buffer's last command
+// A submission still open at an anatomy frame boundary (IssueSwap returned early, or its EndSubmission failed)
+// gets a bottom-of-pipe cb_end for the ending frame and a bottom-of-pipe cb_begin for the next marked frame
+// there, between its commands, so each frame has its own part of it.
+// <anatomy>_gpu.csv: one row per anatomy row (pre/post or before/after pair) and per cb_begin / cb_end, in
+// recording order (a row is written at its post / after mark):
+//   frame        capture frame (the anatomy CSV's frame column)
+//   idx          anatomy row index (cb_begin / cb_end: the next row's index, = rows recorded before the mark)
+//   kind         draw | copy | cb_begin | cb_end
+//   submission   host submission number (as in the gpu_ts timeline events)
+//   gpu_t_us     the pre / before mark (cb rows: the mark), us since the frame's first cb_begin
+//   gpu_prep_us  pre / before minus the previous mark of the same submission (cb_end: the submission's tail,
+//                cb_end minus its last mark; 0 when a copy ended at it). For a submission's first row, the
+//                previous mark is its cb_begin or, when later, the previous submission's cb_end (a top-of-pipe
+//                cb_begin can be written while the previous submission still runs; known when that submission's
+//                cb_end is in the same frame or the frame written before), so prep never includes the previous
+//                submission's work
+//   gpu_exec_us  post minus pre (the draw), after minus before (the whole resolve)
+//   gpu_row_us   prep + exec (cb_end: the tail)
+// <anatomy>_gpu_frames.csv: one row per marked frame: frame, submissions (with both cb marks in this frame),
+// cb_sum_us (cb_end - cb_begin summed over them; may count the overlap of consecutive submissions twice),
+// busy_union_us (the union of those intervals), idle_gap_us (first cb_begin to last cb_end minus busy_union_us),
+// marks, marks_dropped (frame slot full), marks_unavailable (no result: the command never ran, or its
+// submission's command buffer wasn't submitted - those queries aren't read).
+// Empty columns: a mark is missing. Bottom-of-pipe timestamps between draws may keep the GPU from overlapping
+// consecutive draws, so a marked frame can take longer than an unmarked one; compare cb_sum_us with the gpu_ts
+// events of unmarked frames.
